hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18139","Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar and Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, they said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman, from his uncle, Ibn Abi Zaidah said: Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, who said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah pursuing a woman of the Ansar, wanting to look at her. Ibn Abi Zaidah said: Buthaynah daughter of al-Dahhak, wanting to look at her. So I said: You are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, yet you do this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, casts into the heart of a man the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her."
"18140","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah who said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah pursuing Buthaynah daughter of al-Dahhak, sister of Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak, while she was on a rooftop of theirs, and mentioned the hadith."
"18141","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Did any of you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about it? So al-Mughirah ibn Shubah stood and said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judge a sixth for her. He said: Did anyone hear that with you? So Muhammad ibn Maslamah stood and said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judge a sixth for her. So Abu Bakr gave her the sixth."
"18142","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Abi al-Salt informed me, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Ali sent to Muhammad ibn Maslamah, so he was brought. He said: What kept you back from this affair? He said: Your cousin, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me a sword and said: Fight with it while the enemy is fought; but if you see people killing one another, head with it to a rock and strike it with it, then stay in your house until a decisive death comes to you or an erring hand. He said: Let him go."
"18143","Ishaq ibn Sulayman, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas, and Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Uthman ibn Kharashah, my father said, and Ishaq ibn Isa said: From Uthman ibn Kharashah, Abdullah said, and Musab al-Zubayri narrated to us from Malik likewise, and said: Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Kharashah, of Banu Amir ibn Luayy; and none narrated it from al-Zuhri except Malik, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb who said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, asking him for her inheritance. So he said: I know nothing for you in the Book of Allah, nor do I know anything for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until I ask the people. So he asked, and al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, grant her the sixth. He said: Who testifies with you, or who knows with you? So Muhammad ibn Maslamah stood and said likewise, so he granted it to her. And Ishaq ibn Isa said: Is there anyone with you besides you."
"18144","Waki narrated to us, from Thawr, from a man of Basra, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, casts into the heart of a man the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her."
"18145","Abdussamad narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Muslim Abu Umar narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Muawiyah sent us to Ibn al-Zubayr. When I arrived at Madinah, I entered upon so-and-so, Ziyad forgot his name, so he said: The people have done what they have done, so what do you see? He said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, advised me: If you witness any of these tribulations, head to Uhud and break the edge of your sword with it, then sit in your house. He said: If someone enters your house against you, go to the inner room; if he enters the inner room against you, kneel on your knees and say: Bear my sin and your sin, so you will be among the companions of the Fire, and that is the recompense of the wrongdoers. So I have broken the edge of my sword and sat in my house."
